# MANDATORY: TRANSOVO MCTB INFORMATION ARCHITECTURE & NAVIGATION MAP

**Source of truth:** `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-INFORMATION-ARCHITECTURE-AND-NAVIGATION-MAP.md`  
**Prerequisite:** `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-PRODUCT-SCOPE-AND-DOMAIN-RULES.md` (`.cursor/rules/transovo-mctb-product-scope.mdc`)  
**Applies with:** `transovo-mctb-page-manifest.mdc`, `transovo-mctb-canonical.mdc`, all `transovo-*.mdc` standards (always).

## When this rule activates

**Before any work** on MCTB navigation, routing, page placement, sidebar, redirects, or feature discoverability — read product scope first, then **this IA map**, then page manifest, then canonical product map.

Paths include (not exhaustive): `src/components/mctb/**`, `src/app/**/voice/**`, `src/app/**/mctb/**`, `src/lib/products/voice-nav.ts`, `src/lib/mctb/**`, onboarding MCTB routes.

## Authority order (MCTB)

1. `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-PRODUCT-SCOPE-AND-DOMAIN-RULES.md` — what MCTB is / is not
2. **`docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-INFORMATION-ARCHITECTURE-AND-NAVIGATION-MAP.md` — this rule** (where everything lives)
3. `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-PAGE-INVENTORY-AND-ROUTE-MANIFEST.md` — completeness (every page, route, state)
4. `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-CANONICAL-PRODUCT-MAP.md` — domain model, lifecycle, page specs
5. `docs/TRANSOVO-MCTB-PAGE-BUILD-SPECS.md` + route-specific spec — screen implementation
4. All Transovo standards (`transovo-*.mdc`)
5. Existing code and screenshots — evidence only

## Hard requirements

1. **Task-based IA:** Missed Call → Conversation → Follow-up → Recovery. Operational work dominates setup.
2. **Minimal sidebar:** Home | Missed Calls | Conversations | **Voicemail** | Analytics | Setup (+ Numbers under Configure; Settings org-wide). **Voicemail is a permanent operational peer** (locked per build spec 05).
3. **Setup is grouped** — Phone, Messaging, Consent, Schedule, Voicemail **configuration**, Exclusions, Test live inside Setup. Voicemail **inbox** is `/mctb/voicemail`, not buried in Setup.
4. **One canonical home** per feature. One canonical label. No duplicate management surfaces.
5. **Canonical prefix:** `/mctb/*` (legacy `/voice/*` → redirects during migration).
6. **Operational vs config:** Overview/Missed Calls/Conversations/Analytics = daily work. Everything else = setup, audit, process, or admin.
7. **Filters ≠ nav** — Needs attention, Today, Replied, Suppressed are filters, not sidebar items.
8. **Try It / Test** → Setup → Test. Onboarding is temporary process nav, not sidebar.
9. **Consent Log** → compliance/audit (Setup → Compliance or contextual detail), not default primary nav.
10. **Number roles separated** — Business line | Forwarding destination | Text-back sender. Never "Your number."
11. **Cross-link, don't duplicate** — Missed Call ↔ Conversation ↔ Contact. One thread editor.
12. **One nav source of truth** — central MCTB nav config; do not hard-code sidebar per page.
13. **Legacy routes** — inventory/redirects only; Voice/Agent John architecture does not define MCTB IA.

## Canonical route map (target)

```
/mctb                          Home
/mctb/missed-calls[/:id]
/mctb/conversations[/:id]
/mctb/voicemail[/:id]
/mctb/analytics
/mctb/setup[/phone|messaging|consent|schedule|voicemail|exclusions|test]
/mctb/compliance[/consent]
/f/mctb/:token                 Public request form (no admin nav)
/onboarding/mctb               Temporary process only
```

## Page classification gate

Before adding any MCTB page, classify as: **operational workspace | object detail | configuration | audit/compliance | temporary process | public/customer | admin/support**. Then place per this map.

## Governing sentence

MCTB navigation answers: **who called → did we text → did they reply → do I follow up → is it configured** — with operational surfaces prominent and configuration grouped under Setup.
